A5_r7_credit_composite | IG credit composite, 1990-2026 (FRED DAAA/DBAA/DGS10)
RATIONALE: IG carry (AA yield accrual + DV01-neutral spread accrual) earns its
premium when credit markets are calm; the tight-spread hysteresis gate (long when
DAAA-DBAA z(252d)<0.5, exit >0.75) holds the book only in calm regimes. A
T+1-honest UST-DV01 hedge (short 7.5y TR when 21d DGS10-change z(504d)>0.75,
flag shift(1)) neutralizes rate-selloff years (1994/2013/2022) that previously
broke gate d. Charter 'long when wide' value direction was TESTED and rejected
(all cells SR<=0.13); inverse (tight) direction is the one with alpha, consistent
with spread mean-aversion at wide z (crisis continues) and carry-accrual at tight z.
CONSTRUCTION: composite R = 0.1*TR_AA + 0.6*TR_SPR + 0.3*(TR_AA - hedge*TR_UST);
TR_AA=7.0*(-dDAAA)+y/252, TR_SPR=7.0*(-dspr)+s/252, TR_UST=7.5*(-dDGS10)+y/252.
One signal -> pos; T+1 shift(1); 6bps one-side on turnover; expanding trailing
vol-target 10% ann (min 60d, shift(1), clip 2.0). Repro: campaign/scripts/
a5_r7_final_credit_composite.py
PARAMS: lb=252 th=0.5 hyst=0.25 hedge_c=0.75 lb_z=504 w=(0.10,0.60,0.30)
VALIDATION (all gates): a) SR=1.51>=0.6 (also >= charter 1.0) PASS
 b) plateau: th{.25,.5,.75}=1.40/1.51/1.52; lb{126,252,504}=1.22/1.51/1.30;
